Relevant columns and why they matter  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.diseaseId`: identify records that refer to pancreatic endocrine carcinoma (`EFO_0007416`).  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.status`: keep only drugs whose trials are marked **Completed**.  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.prefName`: readable drug name.  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.approvedSymbol`: HGNC‑approved symbol of the drug’s main target.  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.urls.list.element.url`: links to the individual ClinicalTrials.gov (or other) records.  
• `knownDrugsAggregated.drugId`: technical identifier that lets us join to the molecule table if we want extra molecular details (name, description, etc.).  
• `molecule.name`: alternative drug name, useful to double‑check or enrich the output.  

Typical conditions  
• `WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'` – match pancreatic endocrine carcinoma.  
• `AND status = 'Completed'` – only trials that have finished.  
• Optional `AND phase >= 1` or similar when you want to restrict phases.  

Below are ten progressively richer inspection queries (each limited to 20 rows) that explore the data and culminate in the required answer.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct clinical‑trial statuses recorded in knownDrugsAggregated
SELECT DISTINCT status
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick look at drugs associated with pancreatic endocrine carcinoma
SELECT drugId, prefName, phase, status
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Same list, but keep only COMPLETED trials
SELECT drugId, prefName, phase, status
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND status = 'Completed'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Show target gene symbols together with the drugs
SELECT drugId, prefName, approvedSymbol, phase, status
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND status = 'Completed'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect raw URL objects that store links to clinical‑trial pages
SELECT drugId,
       prefName,
       url_struct.element.url AS trial_url
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(k.urls.list) AS url_struct
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND status = 'Completed'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Aggregate all trial links per drug (array of URLs)
WITH trials AS (
  SELECT drugId,
         ARRAY_AGG(url_struct.element.url) AS trial_urls
  FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
  CROSS JOIN UNNEST(k.urls.list) AS url_struct
  WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
    AND status = 'Completed'
  GROUP BY drugId
)
SELECT *
FROM trials
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Join to the molecule table to pick the molecule's canonical name
SELECT k.drugId,
       m.name        AS molecule_name,
       k.prefName    AS pref_name_in_knownDrugs,
       k.approvedSymbol
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
LEFT JOIN `open-targets-prod.platform.molecule`            AS m
       ON k.drugId = m.id
WHERE k.diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND k.status = 'Completed'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. One‑liner that already gives name, target symbol and one example URL
SELECT k.prefName                  AS drug_name,
       k.approvedSymbol            AS target_symbol,
       url_struct.element.url      AS any_trial_url
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(k.urls.list) AS url_struct
WHERE k.diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND k.status = 'Completed'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as #8 but make the URL list unique and compact
SELECT k.prefName                               AS drug_name,
       k.approvedSymbol                         AS target_symbol,
       ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT url_struct.element.url) AS trial_urls
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(k.urls.list) AS url_struct
WHERE k.diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'
  AND k.status = 'Completed'
GROUP BY k.prefName, k.approvedSymbol
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL answer: drugs with COMPLETED trials for pancreatic endocrine carcinoma,
--     including drug name, target symbol and full list of clinical‑trial URLs.
SELECT
  k.prefName                                  AS drug_name,
  k.approvedSymbol                            AS target_symbol,
  ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT url_struct.element.url
            ORDER BY url_struct.element.url)  AS clinical_trial_urls
FROM `open-targets-prod.platform.knownDrugsAggregated` AS k
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(k.urls.list) AS url_struct
WHERE k.diseaseId = 'EFO_0007416'          -- pancreatic endocrine carcinoma
  AND k.status   = 'Completed'             -- only completed studies
GROUP BY k.prefName, k.approvedSymbol
LIMIT 20;
```

